<h2>The 18–24 day transit changes what you should ship how</h2>
<p>This is the longest major transit we quote, and it has real consequences for perishables. Grapes need flawless pre-cooling and SO₂ pad management to survive it with useful shelf life remaining on arrival. For non-perishable products like guar gum and dehydrated onion, the long transit is a non-issue — just a planning input for inventory timing.</p>

